# `docs/AS_BUILT.md merge=union` USED TO LIVE HERE, AND IT IS GONE ON PURPOSE.
#
# Union is git's built-in "keep both sides of a conflicting hunk, never report a
# conflict" driver. That was correct for exactly as long as the file was
# APPEND-ONLY: every change added an entry at the top, so two branches conflicted
# by construction rather than by subject and "keep both" was always the right
# resolution.
#
# `docs/AS_BUILT.md` is now FROZEN (see the note at its top, `docs/AS_BUILT.md:5`),
# and the live record is one file per change under `docs/as-built/`. Two separate
# files never conflict with each other, so there is nothing left for union to
# resolve — and on a frozen file the attribute is actively harmful: union NEVER
# raises, so any edit that reaches this file at all would be silently doubled
# instead of stopping someone. A file nobody may write wants the LOUDEST merge
# behaviour available, which is git's default.
#
# The rule that replaces it is not an attribute at all, because attributes are
# not run server-side by GitHub: `scripts/ci/as-built-write-guard.sh` fails any
# branch whose base…head diff touches `docs/AS_BUILT.md`, and
# `scripts/ci/check-governed-repo-attributes.ts` fails if a tracked attributes
# rule ever assigns that path a merge driver again.
